Mg is a Micro (GNU) Emacs: small, fast, portable Emacs-like editor,
public domain, created 1987 from MicroEMACS v30.

This is the troglobit fork, tracking OpenBSD mg upstream and adding new
usability features: UTF-8 (multibyte type/display/edit, Unicode 17),
syntax highlighting with file modes (c, cmake, conf, diff, git-commit,
markdown, python, shell-script, yaml...), quick help C-h q with a
built-in tutorial (C-h t), M-; comment-dwim, line numbers, buffer
cycling C-x Left/Right, ido-style prompts, dired.

Packaged as mg-troglobit to live beside the stock editors/mg snapshots:
same binary name (bin/mg), declared CONFLICTS_INSTALL.  Ships the full
doc payload: tutorial.md (found by C-h t), Markus Kuhn's utf8.txt
sample as a rendering testbench, and the upstream .mg example config at
share/examples/mg/dot-mg.
WWW: https://github.com/troglobit/mg
